From cb5ef82de3b04b613658b63586224398c1d9ff76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:31:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Whole test suite on the GPU: MFEM_MGIS_DEVICE and fixes of
 the GPU path

The MFEM device may be given by the environment variable MFEM_MGIS_DEVICE,
used by `initialize` when the option --device is not given: the whole
test suite can be run on a GPU (`MFEM_MGIS_DEVICE=cuda ctest -j 1`, with or
without the variables forcing the computations by kernels). The first run
revealed defects of the GPU path:

- ParaviewExportResults referenced the unknowns (`MakeTRef`): without
  prolongation, the true vector of MFEM only wraps the memory of the host,
  and `SetFromTrueVector` copied the stale values of the host over the
  unknowns computed on the device. The export now copies the unknowns in
  its own grid function (`SetFromTrueDofs`) and writes the values of the
  host. The solutions of TwoLayerCube, UniaxialTensileTest and the
  micromorphic tests were wrong on the GPU after a post-processing.
- computeL2ErrorAgainstAnalyticalSolution and GridFunctionInterpolator
  read on the host values computed on the device: they are now
  synchronised.
- The `Elasticity` strategy of BoomerAMG, not supported by hypre on a GPU
  (abort of MFEM), falls back to the `System` strategy with a warning.
- HypreILU: `mfem::HypreILU::SetOperator` creates a new preconditioner of
  hypre with the default options of MFEM (level of fill of one): the
  option `HypreILULevelOfFill` was lost from the second operator on, also
  on the CPU. The preconditioner now applies its settings again after each
  operator. The factorisations with a level of fill greater than zero make
  hypre crash on a GPU (hypre 3.0.2, CUDA 13): the level of fill is zero
  by default there, and greater levels are refused with a message.
- `isHypreUsingGPU`, whose result, contrary to the inline
  `mfem::HypreUsingGPU`, does not depend on the headers of hypre included
  by the caller.

Tests: HypreILUTest (level of fill kept after a new operator, ILU(0) by
default and greater levels refused on a GPU; the loss of the settings is
detected by mutation). Tests made portable to a device: reads on the host
after synchronisation (OperatorSmoothersTest, GridFunctionInterpolatorTest),
problem destroyed before the release of the device
(PartialQuadratureFunctionTest), ILU(0) on a GPU (TwoLayerCube,
UniaxialTensileTest, unit tests utilities), numbers of iterations of
hypre and of the accelerations of the fixed point compared with margins on
a GPU, where the sums are not deterministic (HypreBoomerAMGTest,
FixedPointSolverTest).

Results on a RTX 5080: the whole suite passes on the GPU, with the default
computations and with all the computations forced to the kernels (145/147,
the two failures being the tests which require no device, DeviceForallTest-
cpu and DeviceOptionTest-none); 157/157 on the CPU.
